  "interpretation": "Optional bounded FIFO cache reuses admitted surviving HP translations in both eager enumeration and lazy expansions. Every chance trace is reused unchanged; KO-boundary predictions fall back to the engine. Both arms have the same actual-engine-work and time limits, so cached arms may expand additional chance mass. One run per policy and arm is a performance diagnostic, not a precise speed estimate or a policy-strength claim. The cache is disabled by default. Full-information first-decision bounds do not certify the deployed blind policy."
